                            "Biochemie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "936c27f3-b4a4-4d49-8dea-2a80fd1c94b0",
                                "sense_id": "a04b6db1-8ba1-33b4-83bf-d8af673805eb",
                                "text": "Cytosin ist ein chemischer Baustein von DNA- bzw. RNA-Sequenzen."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b85b5f7a-a80b-4932-ac6f-2db6ed3168a0",
                        "source_entry_id": "d84c6b5a-e9ea-37aa-bfb0-44b249f72c70",
                        "source_sense_id": "a04b6db1-8ba1-33b4-83bf-d8af673805eb",
                        "source_sense_description": "Biochemie: Nukleinbase und Pyrimidin-Derivat",
                        "target_lang_word": "cytosine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cytosine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "735a2fb7-4ffb-338d-aeff-d011f3df1847",
                                        "entry_id": "589fb96a-50c5-33d9-a522-36a69d854e69",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A heterocyclic base, 4-aminopyrimidin-2(1H)-one, which pairs with guanine in DNA and RNA (by means of three hydrogen bonds)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f9f34ce-e130-4ee1-8bca-94d672bd90d0",
                                                "sense_id": "735a2fb7-4ffb-338d-aeff-d011f3df1847",
                                                "text": "Then he found them, the substances that made up the four-letter alphabet in whose language all life is written — adenine and cytosine, guanine and thymine."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7d5fde11-aa3b-4ac4-9822-f7b8672d83a9",
                        "source_entry_id": "d84c6b5a-e9ea-37aa-bfb0-44b249f72c70",
                        "source_sense_id": "a04b6db1-8ba1-33b4-83bf-d8af673805eb",
                        "source_sense_description": "Biochemie: Nukleinbase und Pyrimidin-Derivat",
                        "target_lang_word": "cytosine",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cytosine",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b435df0-41b3-32a3-8a62-2a3f6f4e995b",
                                        "entry_id": "bb7ed356-c1a4-3ef2-a213-e6249ac72d70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Base azotée qu’on trouve dans l’ADN et l’ARN, constituée d'un squelette de pyrimidine avec un groupement amine et un groupement cétone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04becc96-c2b0-42b1-993b-41714c67cdee",
                                                "sense_id": "6b435df0-41b3-32a3-8a62-2a3f6f4e995b",
                                                "text": "Les lésions les plus fréquentes sont la perte de base (la formation de sites dépurinés/dépyrimidinés ou abasiques), la déanimation des cytosines ainsi que la production de photoproduits (201-203)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e84c4731-61e0-40be-b24e-824dcdfdd6cb",
                                                "sense_id": "6b435df0-41b3-32a3-8a62-2a3f6f4e995b",
                                                "text": "Nous avons vu comment le métabisulfite de sodium transformait une cytosine en uracile par désamination."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "249a4d17-f6d4-4dd6-9657-2e8617477177",
                        "source_entry_id": "d84c6b5a-e9ea-37aa-bfb0-44b249f72c70",
                        "source_sense_id": "a04b6db1-8ba1-33b4-83bf-d8af673805eb",
                        "source_sense_description": "Biochemie: Nukleinbase und Pyrimidin-Derivat",
                        "target_lang_word": "cytosine",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cytosine",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "464ad629-6aee-3a65-b107-1413d5cc9c12",
                                        "entry_id": "32dc9bd9-e951-3c97-be57-53455d68cce4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "een van de vier nucleotiden (stikstofbasen) die men in DNA en RNA kan vinden"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "928b5fff-7243-4e89-8c69-d9426843eea2",
                                                "sense_id": "464ad629-6aee-3a65-b107-1413d5cc9c12",
                                                "text": "Dat zijn Cytosine (aangeduid met C), Guanine (G), Adenosine (A) en Thymine (T). Tussen haakjes vier belangrijke letters. De kunstenaar: „G, C, A, T (ti ook wel in het absolute notensysteem aangeduid als de noot B). Als letters muzieknoten worden, bepaalt de volgorde van deze noten mijn persoonlijke identiteit."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "909ade15-422e-4f99-b37c-02a86dc45890",
                        "source_entry_id": "d84c6b5a-e9ea-37aa-bfb0-44b249f72c70",
                        "source_sense_id": "a04b6db1-8ba1-33b4-83bf-d8af673805eb",
                        "source_sense_description": "Biochemie: Nukleinbase und Pyrimidin-Derivat",
